Thank you for using Leaf Alert, the plant identification and watering reminder app. Your privacy is important to us, and we are committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your data when you use our app.

By using Leaf Alert, you agree to the terms outlined in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with these terms, please do not use the app.

1. Information We Collect
a. User-Provided Information
Plant Photos: When you use the plant identification feature, you may upload photos of plants. These photos are processed by the Plant.id API (provided by Kindwise) to identify the plant species.

Account Information: If you create an account, we may collect your name, email address, and other optional details you provide.

Reminder Preferences: You may set watering reminders for your plants, which require us to store information about your plants and your preferred watering schedules.

b. Automatically Collected Information
Usage Data: We collect information about how you interact with the app, such as the features you use, the frequency of use, and any errors or crashes.

Device Information: We may collect information about your device, including the device type, operating system, and unique device identifiers.

c. Third-Party Services
Plant.id API: Leaf Alert uses the Plant.id API from Kindwise to identify plants. When you upload a photo, it is sent to Kindwise’s servers for processing. Kindwise’s privacy policy applies to their handling of your data. You can review their privacy policy here.

2. How We Use Your Information
We use the information we collect for the following purposes:

To provide plant identification services and watering reminders.

To improve the functionality and user experience of the app.

To communicate with you about updates, features, or support requests.

To analyze app usage and troubleshoot issues.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. However, we may share your information in the following circumstances:

With Kindwise (Plant.id API): Your plant photos are shared with Kindwise to provide plant identification services.

Service Providers: We may share data with third-party service providers who assist us in operating the app (e.g., hosting, analytics, or customer support).

Legal Requirements: We may disclose your information if required by law or to protect our rights, property, or safety.

4. Data Retention
We retain your information only for as long as necessary to provide the services you requested or as required by law. For example:

Plant photos are temporarily stored for processing and are not retained after identification.

Account information and reminder preferences are stored until you delete your account or request data deletion.

5. Your Rights and Choices
You have the following rights regarding your data:

Access and Correction: You can access and update your account information within the app.

Data Deletion: You can delete your account and associated data at any time.

Opt-Out of Communications: You can unsubscribe from promotional emails by following the instructions in the email.

6. Security
We take reasonable measures to protect your data from unauthorized access, loss, or misuse. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

7. Children’s Privacy
Leaf Alert is not intended for use by children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we become aware that we have collected such information, we will take steps to delete it.

8. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will notify you through the app or via email. Your continued use of Leaf Alert after any changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated policy.

